/* book Worked example: Q: A step-index fiber has n₁ = 1.48, n₂ = 1.46, core radius a = 25 µm and is used at λ = 1.30 µm. Find (a) Δ, exact and approximate; (b) NA; (c) V; (d) the number of modes. (e) A parabolic graded-index fiber has the same n₁, n₂ and a. How many modes does it carry, and what is its index at r = 10 µm?
   1. (a) Exact: Δ = (2.1904 − 2.1316)/(2 × 2.1904) = 0.0588/4.3808 = 0.01342. Approximate: (1.48 − 1.46)/1.48 = 0.01351.
   2. (b) NA = √0.0588 = 0.2425.
   3. (c) 2πa/λ = 2π × 25/1.30 = 157.08/1.30 = 120.83, so V = 120.83 × 0.2425 = 29.30.
   4. (d) V = 29.30 > 2.405, so the fiber is multimode. M ≈ V²/2 = 858.5/2 = 429 modes.
   5. (e) Graded, α = 2, same on-axis NA and radius, so the same V: M ≈ V²/4 = 858.5/4 = 215 modes.
   6. Index at r = 10 µm: (r/a)² = (10/25)² = 0.16, so n = 1.48 × √(1 − 2 × 0.01342 × 0.16) = 1.48 × √0.99571 = 1.48 × 0.99785 = 1.4768.
   7. Check at r = a: n = 1.48 × √(1 − 2 × 0.01342) = 1.48 × √0.97316 = 1.48 × 0.98649 = 1.4600 = n₂, so the exact Δ makes the profile meet the cladding.
   Answer: Δ = 0.01342 (0.01351 approximately), NA = 0.2425, V = 29.3; the step-index fiber carries about 429 modes and the parabolic graded fiber about 215, whose index is 1.4768 at r = 10 µm. */
