/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In communication fibers n₁ and n₂ differ by well under 1 %, so the fiber is weakly guiding and its exact modes group into nearly degenerate sets called linearly polarized (LP) modes, labelled LPlm.
   - So a step-index fiber is single-mode when
   - a is the core radius, λ the vacuum wavelength (same unit), NA = √(n₁² − n₂²).
   - Below 2.405 only LP₀₁ travels, in two polarizations.
   - Set V = 2.405 and solve for λ.
   - λc has the unit of a.
   - Take a = 4 µm and NA = 0.11.
   - Designers place λc below the shortest working wavelength with some margin.
   - The LP₀₁ field is close to a Gaussian and reaches into the cladding.
   - With one mode there is no intermodal dispersion, so single-mode fiber carries the highest bit rates over the longest spans; the price is a laser source and tight alignment of a core only about 9 µm wide.
*/
