/* book Worked example: Q: A step-index fiber has core radius a = 4.0 µm and NA = 0.11. (a) Find its cutoff wavelength. (b) Is it single-mode at 1.31 µm? Support the answer with V.
   1. 2πa·NA = 2π × 4.0 µm × 0.11 = 2.765 µm.
   2. λc = 2.765 µm / 2.405 = 1.150 µm.
   3. At 1.31 µm: V = 2.765/1.31 = 2.110.
   4. 2.110 < 2.405, so only LP₀₁ is guided. Equivalently, 1.31 µm is longer than λc = 1.150 µm.
   Answer: λc = 1.15 µm; at 1.31 µm V = 2.11 < 2.405, so the fiber is single-mode. */
