/* book Worked example 2: Q: Design: a single-mode fiber is to have n₁ = 1.48 and Δ = 0.003, and its cutoff must not exceed 1.26 µm. Find NA, the largest core radius allowed, and, for a = 4.1 µm, the cutoff and V at 1.31 µm and 1.55 µm.
   1. NA = n₁√(2Δ) = 1.48 × √0.006 = 1.48 × 0.07746 = 0.1146.
   2. λc ≤ 1.26 µm needs a ≤ 2.405 λc/(2π NA) = 2.405 × 1.26/(2π × 0.1146) = 3.030/0.7203 = 4.21 µm.
   3. With a = 4.1 µm: 2πa·NA = 2π × 4.1 × 0.1146 = 2.953 µm, so λc = 2.953/2.405 = 1.228 µm, inside the limit.
   4. V at 1.31 µm = 2.953/1.31 = 2.25; V at 1.55 µm = 2.953/1.55 = 1.91. Both are below 2.405.
   5. Check: λc = 1.228 µm is below 1.31 µm, so both windows are single-mode, as the V values say.
   Answer: NA = 0.115 and a must not exceed 4.21 µm; with a = 4.1 µm the cutoff is 1.23 µm and V is 2.25 at 1.31 µm and 1.91 at 1.55 µm. */
