/* book exam traps: Single-mode needs λ longer than λc. A wavelength shorter than cutoff makes V larger than 2.405 and the fiber multimode. | 2.405 is the LP₁₁ cutoff (first zero of J₀). LP₀₁ has no cutoff, so a fiber never guides zero modes. | V is dimensionless and uses the radius a. Writing V in µm, or using the diameter, is a common slip. | λc depends only on a and NA, not on power, fiber length or connectors. | A fiber 'single-mode at 1310 nm' has λc below 1310 nm, not equal to it. */
