/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A guided mode at one frequency varies as ej(ωt − βz).
   - vp is the phase velocity in m/s; ω the angular frequency in rad/s; β the propagation constant in rad/m; c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m/s; neff = β/k₀ the mode's effective index.
   - A single unchanging frequency carries no information: it has no start, no end and no bits.
   - Two waves at nearby frequencies ω ± Δω add to a carrier inside a slowly varying envelope.
   - the slope of the ω–β curve at the carrier frequency.
   - Write β = 2πneff/λ and differentiate with respect to ω (using dλ/dω = −λ²/2πc).
   - vg = c/Ng, Ng = neff − λ dneff/dλ Ng is the group index (dimensionless); dneff/dλ is the slope of the effective index with wavelength.
   - A pulse launched into a fiber of length L arrives after the group delay
   - τ in seconds, L in metres.
   - If Ng itself changes with wavelength, the different wavelengths in a pulse arrive at different times and the pulse spreads.
*/
