/* book Worked example: Q: At λ = 1550 nm a fiber mode has neff = 1.46 and Ng = 1.48. With c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m/s, find (a) the phase velocity, (b) the group velocity, (c) the pulse delay over 10 km and how far the envelope lags the crests.
   1. (a) vp = c/neff = 3.00 × 10⁸/1.46 = 2.055 × 10⁸ m/s.
   2. (b) vg = c/Ng = 3.00 × 10⁸/1.48 = 2.027 × 10⁸ m/s.
   3. (c) L = 10 km = 1.0 × 10⁴ m. τ = L/vg = 10⁴/(2.027 × 10⁸) = 4.933 × 10⁻⁵ s = 49.33 µs.
   4. Crest time L/vp = 10⁴ × 1.46/(3.00 × 10⁸) = 48.67 µs, so the envelope lags by 49.33 − 48.67 = 0.67 µs.
   5. Check: the lag equals L(Ng − neff)/c = 10⁴ × 0.02/(3.00 × 10⁸) = 0.67 µs.
   Answer: vp = 2.05 × 10⁸ m/s, vg = 2.03 × 10⁸ m/s; the pulse takes 49.3 µs over 10 km, 0.67 µs behind the crests. */
