/* book exam traps: Using neff instead of Ng in τ = LNg/c understates the delay; pulses follow the group index. | Phase velocity is not the speed of information; a single unmodulated frequency carries no bits. | Ng = neff − λ dneff/dλ: with a negative slope the two minus signs make Ng larger. Getting Ng below neff in silica points to a sign slip. | Put L in metres: 10 km is 1.0 × 10⁴ m. Keep λ and the slope in matching units (µm and per µm) so the product is a pure number. */
